{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\nDuring the comment-remediation epic, Gerrit briefly advertised `main` with parent `0fe2cc2e…` while Gitiles returned 404 for that object. Ref history appeared rewound and omitted merged commit `2a93f180…`. `git fetch gerrit main` returned timeout/HTTP 504, and CI run `34235734839` failed checkout when Gerrit returned HTTP 502 fetching change 2834. The service later recovered: the parent became readable and ref advertisement worked again.\n\nThis ticket owns the `/rebar-debug` investigation requested by the operator. RCA confirmed the actionable failure class: the pinned `checkout-gerrit-change-action` is mirror-first only when the GitHub mirror exposes the requested Gerrit change ref. Run 34235734839 showed GitHub lacked `refs/changes/34/2834/1`, forcing Gerrit fallback; the fallback returned HTTP 502 before repository validation. A later check found the ref visible on GitHub, proving the versioned refspec can work but that the live mirror can lag/miss until replication is triggered. The operator approved Option A: publish `refs/changes/*` to the org-private GitHub mirror and preserve the pinned action's mirror-first path.\n\n## Operator ruling\nProceed with Option A and use push spec `+refs/changes/*:refs/changes/*`. This is an explicit accepted trade-off for the change-ref namespace only: branch/tag history remains non-force; `refs/meta/config` remains unreplicated via `replicatePermissions = false` and by avoiding wildcard `refs/*`. The force applies to patchset refs and `refs/changes/NN/NNNN/meta`; it is not what creates a missing ref, but it ensures the full replication sweep converges the mirrored change namespace even if Gerrit rewrites change metadata while preserving the one-way-door guard for `main`, tags, and feature branches.\n\n## Plan\n- Record the RCA/timeline on the ticket: run 34235734839 failed before validation because GitHub lacked `refs/changes/34/2834/1`; Gerrit fallback returned 502; recheck run 34236969595 later passed; current mirror checks show the change-ref namespace can be published.\n- Update only the Gerrit change-ref replication spec to the operator-approved forced refspec `+refs/changes/*:refs/changes/*`, keeping `refs/heads/main`, `refs/tags/*`, `refs/heads/feature/*`, `projects = rebar`, `mirror = false`, and `replicatePermissions = false` intact.\n- Add a narrow repository test that parses `infra/gerrit/replication.config` and proves the exact forced change-ref refspec is present while the branch/tag/feature refspecs and privacy/safety filters remain unchanged.\n- Apply the repository config on the Gerrit host through the supported replication setup/materialization path, snapshotting the live `replication.config` first. Use `docker compose exec gerrit gerrit plugin reload replication` if the plugin accepts reload; if not, use the minimal documented Gerrit restart only to load the config.\n- Trigger full replication for remote `github` with the repo-documented Gerrit command `replication start --all --remote github --now --wait`, run from the host/container admin context (for example `docker compose exec gerrit ssh -p 29418 <admin>@localhost replication start --all --remote github --now --wait`, or the equivalent configured admin SSH). This is distinct from plugin reload: reload loads config; the replication start command backfills missing refs because `replicateOnStartup=false` deliberately does not do so.\n- Monitor replication output/disk/CPU enough to catch obvious initial-load failures.\n- Verify `refs/changes/*` visibility on GitHub with `git ls-remote`, spot-check an open change ref, and prove a CI-style `git fetch origin <refs/changes/...>` succeeds from the GitHub mirror without contacting Gerrit.\n- Watch the first Mirror Guard run after the change and confirm it stays green with no replication-lag alarm.\n\n## Testing\n- RED: `pytest tests/scripts/test_gerrit_replication_config.py::<new refs_changes_refspec test>` fails before the config change because the file uses non-forced `refs/changes/*:refs/changes/*`.\n- GREEN targeted: `pytest tests/scripts/test_gerrit_replication_config.py` plus `make config-check`.\n- Final repository verification: `make verify PYTEST_WORKERS=2` with ambient GIT_CONFIG_* variables unset.\n- Operational verification: after host apply and replication, `git ls-remote https://github.com/navapbc/rebar 'refs/changes/*'` returns change refs and a local fresh repo can `git fetch origin <open-change-ref>` from GitHub only.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The incident timeline is recorded on this ticket with exact Gerrit and CI evidence.\n- [ ] The root cause is recorded on this ticket: the mirror-first action fell back to Gerrit because the GitHub mirror lacked the requested change ref at validation time.\n- [ ] The versioned Gerrit replication config publishes `+refs/changes/*:refs/changes/*` while retaining main/tag/feature replication and refs/meta/config privacy controls.\n- [ ] The live Gerrit host has the updated replication config applied and full replication has been triggered successfully.\n- [ ] `refs/changes/*` visibility and a CI-style origin fetch are verified from the GitHub mirror without contacting Gerrit.\n- [ ] Mirror Guard remains green after the change and no replication-lag alarm is observed."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788934861306611001,"uuid":"fbfe5bcb-7b69-4250-b521-6a0f4a3d0d25"}